  "result": "The refusal is decided in `createWebhook` in `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts`. It calls `countEndpoints`, then `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"webhooks\", used)`, and throws `Plan ${org.plan} allows ${used} webhook endpoints` when that returns true. The per-plan webhook cap is declared in `src/config/plan-limits.ts`, in the `PLAN_LIMITS` table (`webhooks: 0`, `2`, `10`, and `UNLIMITED` for the top tier). `wouldExceedLimit` and `getLimit` live in the same file and do the actual comparison against that number.\n\nThe settings UI (`src/app/(dashboard)/[orgSlug]/settings/webhooks/webhook-manager.tsx`) only displays the quota message and disables the form; it does not make the decision.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/webhook-service.ts, src/config/plan-limits.ts",
